---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import '../../styles/lab.css';
---
<SiteLayout title="About — Worldeology Lab" description="Why Worldeology Lab exists and what Cognitive AI means as a research field." headerTone="paper" active="about" image="/og.png">
  <main id="main" class="lab-site lab-page">
    <header class="lab-page-hero"><p class="lab-index">Worldeology Lab / About</p><h1>Why<br />Worldeology?</h1><p>A world is not only physical state. It is also what agents believe, value, remember, choose, and make possible for one another.</p></header>
    <section class="lab-page-section" aria-labelledby="name-title"><header><p class="lab-index">01 / The name</p><h2 id="name-title">World + logos: studying the worlds intelligence participates in creating.</h2></header><div class="lab-prose"><p>Worldeology names a research stance. An intelligent system cannot be understood only through the answer it emits or the benchmark it passes. Its interpretation changes its action; its action changes another agent; those changes accumulate into a different world.</p><p>Cognitive AI is the technical program that makes this trajectory modelable: minds before action, cognition during action, and consequences after action.</p></div></section>
    <section class="lab-page-section" aria-labelledby="principles-title"><header><p class="lab-index">02 / Principles</p><h2 id="principles-title">How we choose research problems.</h2></header>
      <div class="lab-principles">
        <article><b>01</b><h3>Trajectories over snapshots</h3><p>An isolated output hides how understanding formed and what the action later changed.</p></article>
        <article><b>02</b><h3>Hypotheses over mind reading</h3><p>Latent-state models must remain uncertain, revisable, and distinguishable from claims about a person.</p></article>
        <article><b>03</b><h3>Process before post-hoc explanation</h3><p>The useful intervention point is where cognition diverges, not only where the final answer becomes visibly wrong.</p></article>
        <article><b>04</b><h3>Consequences over local appeal</h3><p>A pleasant response can still reduce agency, damage trust, or close a valuable future path.</p></article>
        <article><b>05</b><h3>World models beyond physics</h3><p>Beliefs, goals, relationships, roles, and institutions are part of the state that determines what happens next.</p></article>
        <article><b>06</b><h3>Science that leaves instruments behind</h3><p>Concepts become useful when they produce systems, datasets, evaluations, and falsifiable experiments.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="lab-page-section" aria-labelledby="status-title"><header><p class="lab-index">03 / Status</p><h2 id="status-title">A lab and a field under construction.</h2></header><div class="lab-prose"><p>Worldeology Lab is an emerging independent research identity founded by Xuanming Zhang. The site distinguishes completed work, active systems, and longer-horizon research proposals. Membership and institutional relationships will be stated only when confirmed.</p></div></section>
    <SiteFooter />
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
